{"id":"u-bcf9c6b8-18ef-4762-8d59-6e4414c751c9","src":"community","title":"Muscle & Strength: 5-Day DB PPL V-Taper Recomp","author":"PointFrankRange","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/VVsFAX-muscle-and-strength-5-day-db-ppl-v-taper-recomp","desc":"The Muscle & Strength: 5-Day Dumbbell PPL V-Taper Recomp is a structured, strength-led training system designed for lifters who want to build muscle while reducing body fat without spending hours in the gym. Built around progressive overload and intelligent volume control, this program prioritizes heavy compound movements, pull-up progression, and shoulder development to create a wider upper body and tighter waistline.\n\nDesigned for early-morning lifters and busy professionals, sessions are capped at 55–65 minutes and require only adjustable dumbbells and a pull-up bar. The program blends mechanical tension, controlled hypertrophy work, and recovery balance to drive measurable progress in strength, physique, and performance over a 6-week cycle.\n\nIf your lifts are increasing and your waist measurement is decreasing, the program is working exactly as intended.\n\nProgram Overview\n\nGoal\n   •   Build lean muscle mass\n   •   Reduce body fat through recomposition\n   •   Improve upper-body width (V-taper development)\n   •   Increase strength across key compound lifts\n\nStructure\n   •   Frequency: 5 training days per week\n   •   Split: Push / Pull / Rest / Legs / Upper / Rest / V-Taper Focus\n   •   Session Length: 55–65 minutes\n   •   Cycle Length: 6 weeks with structured progression\n   •   Equipment Required: Adjustable dumbbells + pull-up bar\nRest between Sets:\n•   Heavy Compounds: 2-3 minutes \n•   Secondary Compounds: 90 - 120 seconds\n•   Isolation / Pump Work: 60 - 90 seconds\n•   Core Work: Planks 45 - 60 sec / Leg Raise 60 - 90 sec\n\nProgression Model\n\nThe program follows a double progression system:\n   •   Work within a defined rep range.\n   •   When the top of the range is achieved across all sets, increase load.\n   •   Continue progressing weekly.","level":["Intermediate","Advanced"],"goals":["Women's"],"equipment":["Dumbbell Only"],"minutes":60,"joins":10,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-08-25T11:11:21.045Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Push (60 Min)","Pull (Strength Focus)","Legs (Heavy Tension)","Upper Hypertrophy","V-Taper / Aesthetic"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"x":4}]},{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Standing Shoulder Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"x":3}]},{"n":"Overhead Extension (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Pull-Up (Weighted)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"x":3}],"note":"Baseline for weighted pull-ups:\nIf you are able to do 8 - 12 body weight pull-ups then add weights. Otherwise swap this out for body weight pull-ups or negatives"},{"n":"Bent Over Row (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Chest Supported Row (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Bicep Curl (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Hammer Curl (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"x":3}]},{"n":"Hanging Leg Raise","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"x":3}],"note":"If you are able to hit 12 reps for all three sets then add weights"}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Romanian Deadlift (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"x":4}]},{"n":"Squat (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Bulgarian Split Squat (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Standing Calf Raise","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"x":4}]},{"n":"Hanging Leg Raise","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"x":2}],"note":"OPTIONAL - If you have not hit 60 minutes and have extra time. Add weights if you consistently max the reps."}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Pull-Up (Bodyweight)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"x":3}],"note":"No weights - Focusing on clean pull-ups and slow negatives"},{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo"